==English==
{{was wotd|2007|April|16}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|sutilté}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|subtīlitās}}, from {{m|la|subtīlis||subtle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsʌtəlti/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-subtlety.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|subtleties}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality or fact of being [[subtle]].
#: ''With all his usual '''subtlety''', he quietly fixed the problem before anyone else noticed it.''
# {{lb|en|countable}} An instance of being [[subtle]], a [[subtle]] thing, especially a subtle [[argument]] or [[distinction]].
#: ''The '''subtleties''' of this overture are often overlooked.''
# {{lb|en|countable}} An ornate medieval illusion dish or table decoration, especially when made from one thing but crafted to look like another.
#: ''At the king's coronation feast, several '''subtleties''' were served between main courses.''

